    "FL-154": {
      "label": "A model configuration and token cost policy per agent type: pinned, max, elbow or floor.",
      "walk": "Open the agent-type config; each type (agent, sub-agent, curator) has its own token-cost policy set to one of pinned, max, elbow or floor.",
      "protected": true,
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "screenshot": "FL-154.png",
      "flag": "",
      "observed": "Three fresh runs display distinct agent, sub-agent, judge and curator policies, initially pinned to GPT-4.1 mini. Sub-agent policy changes to max without changing other roles, then is restored. Every archive, comparison and seed request uses GPT-4.1 mini (receipts/model-proof.json); released 0.1.70 used MiniMax M3 for these same operations."
    },
    "FL-173": {
      "label": "Constitution: a warming retry when the Palace is asleep, a \"busy, retrying\" banner on rate limits, and the banner clears on recovery (gate-day).",
      "walk": "Start the Harness against a sleeping Palace; a warming line shows, then clears when the Palace answers; drop one Palace request on purpose mid-conversation: a read or an idempotent write is retried on its own and the step completes, and only a refusal or a /remember fails at once (owner, 2026-10-07).",
      "protected": true,
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "screenshot": "FL-173.png",
      "flag": "",
      "observed": "F195 busy-response corner: three consecutive fresh runs (5,6,7) on the one-instance test Palace; native loads returned 133/130/132 Cloud Run 429s. Forced 429 and 503 compactions complete, retrying notice clears, Jobs recovers, confirmed deletes replay. Symphony stage and post-judge resolution also complete after forced 429; /remember survives three refusals through the outbox. This is not a new cold-start warming claim. See run results, busy logs, remember and symphony-3/4."
    }
  },
